<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <GenerateAssemblyInfo>true</GenerateAssemblyInfo>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net48</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <AssemblyName>FireflyIIINet</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>FireflyIIINet</PackageId>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <Authors>FireflyIII.Net</Authors>
    <Company>FireflyIII.Net</Company>
    <AssemblyTitle>Firefly III API Client</AssemblyTitle>
    <Description>A .NET client library for the Firefly III API.</Description>
    <RootNamespace>FireflyIIINet</RootNamespace>
    <!-- Version tracks the Firefly III API version (Major.Minor.Patch);
         the 4th revision component is bumped for client-only changes against the same API version. -->
    <Version>6.7.8.1</Version>
    <DocumentationFile>bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\FireflyIIINet.xml</DocumentationFile>
    <!-- CS1591: undocumented members (Refit interfaces); CS8073: value-type != null in generated Equals -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CS8073</NoWarn>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/filipe-silva/FireflyIII.Net</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/filipe-silva/FireflyIII.Net.git</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>6.7.8.1, client-only fixes against Firefly III API 6.7.8, checked against the live demo. Requests send only what the caller set: unset optional fields are no longer sent as null or 0001-01-01, which the server rejected (StoreAccount/UpdateAccount without a currency, StoreTransactionLink without a link type name). Breaking: the bool/int fields of the *Update models are now bool?/int? and left out while null; a rename used to send active:false and deactivate the budget, bill, recurrence, rule group or webhook, and order:0 (rejected for rules). *Store models: active defaults to true (budgets, bills, rule groups and recurrences were created inactive), an unset order is left to the server, and a recurrence repetition's weekend defaults to 1. Piggy banks: PiggyBankAccountStore sends account_id (the server's name; the spec says id), and PiggyBankStore/PiggyBankUpdate gain TransactionCurrencyId/TransactionCurrencyCode, one of which the server requires; piggy banks could not be created before. Responses: string properties accept JSON numbers (ListAvailableBudgets failed), date-only fields accept date-times (every recurrence failed to read), and BudgetProperties.CurrencyDecimalPlaces is int? (a budget without its own currency failed to read). CategoryUpdate.Notes and Color are three-state: unassigned keeps the stored value, null clears it. Docs: Notes = "" clears notes on the other updates; TransactionLinkUpdate and RecurrenceUpdate need fields the spec calls optional; servers behind Cloudflare need a User-Agent; no native AOT. scripts/smoke-test.cs now also reads every top-level list.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Nullable>annotations</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Ship the repo README as the package readme (referenced by PackageReadmeFile above).
         Path is relative to this project (repo root is two levels up). -->
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Refit" />
    <!-- Since Refit 14 the reflection request builder is a separate package; referenced here so
         RestService.For<T> works everywhere (on net48 the source-generated stubs are not resolved,
         so reflection is the only path). Keep version-locked to Refit. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Refit.Reflection" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.ComponentModel.Annotations" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
